With your permission, the CarmaCars app or the website shares where you are with our team only two hours either side of your pickup and your return, so we can meet you. At any other time nothing is taken. Turn it off any time in **Account** > **Notifications** > **Location sharing**.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Your booking is confirmed. A few things are left: your licence photos, a selfie and proof of coverage, a signature from each additional driver, and the deposit.</p><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-what-we-still-need-from-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What we still need from you</h2><p class="gd-p">While a request or booking is not complete, everything it still needs is in one list, <b class="gd-ui">To do</b>, under the steps on <b class="gd-ui">Trips</b> and on the booking: one line for each thing, with its state and a small button. The red button of <b class="gd-ui">Do this next</b> is always the first thing to do.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Needed</td><td>Send it: press the button on the line</td></tr><tr><td>Not accepted</td><td>We could not accept what you sent: the reason is on the line, send it again</td></tr><tr><td>Under review</td><td>We have it and a person on our team is checking it</td></tr><tr><td>Done</td><td>Nothing more to do</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="gd-p">The lines are what this booking needs: your licence (front and back) and a selfie for each driver, proof of coverage (not with the Protection Plan), signing and paying, the deposit, each additional driver accepting the terms, your date of birth and your home address. On the booking, the details the agreement needs are filled in right there, under <b class="gd-ui">Your details for the agreement</b>. Our reminders name the same things.</p><p class="gd-p">Each line says exactly what is missing. With your own insurance (OPCF 27) you send two pages: the <b class="gd-ui">pink slip</b> (the insurance card for your own car) and the <b class="gd-ui">OPCF 27 endorsement page</b> of your policy. If one is missing, the line says which one (&quot;We have your OPCF 27 endorsement page. Still needed: your pink slip&quot;), and its button opens that upload with the page chosen. Next to each upload is an example picture of the page with the parts that must show circled: your name, the policy number, the dates, the insurer and, on the endorsement page, the OPCF 27 line. Find it in your insurer&#39;s app or website, in your email, or in your car&#39;s glovebox. Put it flat, get all four corners in the photo, and avoid glare.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-your-booking-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your booking page</h2><p class="gd-p">Every booking opens with a large photo of your car, its name, the status and a clock: &quot;Pickup in 2 days 4 h&quot;, or &quot;Return by Sun 7 PM&quot; while you have the car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Trips</b>, then your booking. The status is on the photo, for example Confirmed, with your booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Under the photo: when and where you pick up and return the car (tap a place to open it in Maps), the kilometres included, the fuel rule and the deposit.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Do this next</b>, at the top, tells you the one thing still needed, with its red button, for example <b class="gd-ui">Upload documents</b>, and the time left before pickup. Under it, your steps: done, now (<b class="gd-ui">Your turn</b>) and later. When nothing is needed it says when and where to pick up the car, with <b class="gd-ui">Add to calendar</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Manage your trip holds <b class="gd-ui">Licence and coverage</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Extend</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Ask to change dates</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Message us</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Call us</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add a driver</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Cancel booking</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10003</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/972"><img src="/guides/img/renter-08-booking-confirmed-desktop-b5603da5.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="972"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:10.4%;top:54.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:9.4%;top:78.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.4%;top:76.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">Money, on the right (below on a phone), shows what you paid and what is owing, part by part, with a <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b> button when something is open and your receipts. <b class="gd-ui">Price details</b> opens every line of the price. The steps under <b class="gd-ui">Do this next</b> show how far along you are: approve the offer, sign and pay, licence and insurance, pick up, return, final statement. A step finished since your last visit ticks over as the bar moves.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-your-rental-step-by-step" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your rental, step by step</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Your rental, step by step</b> on your booking opens the walkthrough: the whole rental in four stages, Before pickup, At pickup, On the road and The return.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Start the walkthrough</b> (<b class="gd-ui">Continue</b> once you have begun). The top shows how many steps are done and which stage you are at.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The step to do now is in black at the top. A task opens its page, for example <b class="gd-ui">Add your licence</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Sign the agreement</b>, and is ticked once it is done. A step to read (what to bring, where we meet, your own photos, the road rules, what to do if something goes wrong, how to bring the car back) has <b class="gd-ui">Got it</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">At pickup, the walk-around: we photograph the car with you and you sign the condition report on your phone. Once done, <b class="gd-ui">See the photo report</b> opens every photo.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Every stage is listed below with its steps, so you can read ahead.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-upload-your-licence-selfie-and-coverage" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Upload your licence, selfie and coverage</h2><p class="gd-p">Do this at least 24 hours before pickup. It takes a few minutes with your phone.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On your booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Upload documents</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Licence and coverage</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Licence, front: lay the licence on a dark surface with all four corners visible. Press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Choose from my photos</b> for a photo already on your phone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Licence, back: do the same for the back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Selfie with your licence: hold the licence beside your face, then press <b class="gd-ui">Take selfie</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Coverage for damage to the car: add what your option asks for, then press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Choose from my photos</b> (a PDF works too). Not sure your credit card covers rentals? Use the card coverage checker first.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">While your booking still needs them, <b class="gd-ui">Your trips</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Upload your licence</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Upload proof of insurance</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Check if your credit card covers rentals</b>, and our request and offer emails link straight to the licence upload.</p><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10003/verify</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1232"><img src="/guides/img/renter-09-verify-desktop-d20f668d.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1232"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.5%;top:65.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:63.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:81.2%;top:63.6%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:95.3%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Your option</th><th scope="col">What we need</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Option 1, OPCF 27 on your own policy</td><td>Your insurer, the policy number and its expiry (after your return date), then two pages: your <b class="gd-ui">pink slip</b> (the liability insurance card) and the <b class="gd-ui">OPCF 27 endorsement page</b>, each a PDF or a photo. Send both before you pay: the payment opens once they are in.</td></tr><tr><td>Option 2, your credit card&#39;s rental coverage</td><td>Pay with that card: it must be a credit card (debit and prepaid cards are refused) in your name. Search for your card (the bank and the card&#39;s name) and pick it: the page tells you at once whether it covers this car (the card&#39;s value limit, the kinds of car it leaves out, the most days). Then tick and confirm. Not on the list? Tick <b class="gd-ui">My card is not on the list</b> and type its name: our team checks it. The card&#39;s benefits document is optional.</td></tr><tr><td>Option 3, the CarmaCars Protection Plan</td><td>Ask for it on your booking; we confirm it once it is active.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Which cards include rental car coverage? <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage</span> lists them, with each card&#39;s car value limit (MSRP), its longest rental and a link to its guide. Most cards stop at a car priced $65,000 or $85,000, and some of our cars are priced higher. Only your card&#39;s issuer decides a claim: call the number on the back of your card before you rent.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A person checks your proof and approves it, or tells you what to fix. The car is handed over only once it is approved. Changing your option replaces the earlier proof. We remind you 48 and 24 hours before pickup while it is missing. We delete licence and face photos 90 days after your rental ends.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-additional-drivers" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Additional drivers</h2><p class="gd-p">Each additional driver signs the agreement with their own link.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">When the agreement is ready, each driver with an email gets their own signing link.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On your booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Copy their signing link</b> to send it yourself, or <b class="gd-ui">Send a new link</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each driver adds their own licence photos and selfie, like you did.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Signing links expire after 72 hours. A new link ends the older one, so always send the newest.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-add-something-to-your-trip" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add something to your trip</h2><p class="gd-p">Until 24 hours before pickup (or the notice an add-on needs), add add-ons from your booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On your booking, under Add-ons, press <b class="gd-ui">Add something to your trip</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Tick the add-on you want. Its price shows below.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add and pay</b>. It is charged at once on the card you paid with, and shows on your booking and receipt.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A chauffeur needs our confirmation: press <b class="gd-ui">Ask for it</b>. We confirm it and charge your card then.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">No card on file for this booking? The add-on is added and waits for payment: press <b class="gd-ui">Pay for your add-ons</b> under Add-ons, enter a card and press <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b>. It is charged at once; that card is not kept.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>If you cancel, add-ons are refunded like the rest of your booking. Flowers and a chauffeur are not refunded once their notice before pickup has started.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-what-to-bring-to-pickup" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What to bring to pickup</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Your original licence. A photo is not enough.</li><li>The card you paid with. The deposit is taken on it about an hour before pickup.</li><li>A few minutes to walk around the car with us. We photograph it together.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-check-in-yourself-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check in yourself (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">From 24 hours before pickup, <b class="gd-ui">Check in yourself</b> on your booking: take the photos of the car as you get it (pick them all at once from your camera roll: all sides, odometer, fuel gauge, inside, any damage), the odometer and the fuel. If your booking is ready, you are checked in at once; otherwise a team member confirms it. If you do not take the photos, we take them.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-if-we-change-your-coverage-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">If we change your coverage (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">If your card does not cover the car, or you ask for the CarmaCars Protection Plan, our team can switch your booking for you. You get an email with what changed and the new total. On an offer you approve the new price. On a booking you have paid, any extra is sent to you as a secure payment link, or you pay it from your booking page. You then do not need to send a card coverage document. If you go back to your card, the booking page asks you to confirm it again.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-your-accident-card" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your accident card</h2><p class="gd-p">Your booking shows your <b class="gd-ui">Accident card</b>: what to do after an accident, and the coverage of this booking.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>With your own auto policy (OPCF 27): your insurer and policy number, as on the proof you uploaded.</li><li>With your credit card coverage: the card and its coverage provider.</li><li>With the Protection Plan: the provider, the policy number, the claims phone and your plan reference.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Print it</b> to print the card at its size for the glovebox, or keep the page on your phone.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Your name and date of birth</h3><p class="gd-p">Set them in your profile. Once your licence is verified they must match it: a change is sent as a correction request, shown as waiting until our team checks it against your licence.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-if-your-card-does-not-cover-the-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">If your card does not cover the car</h2><p class="gd-p">The page says why: the card has no rental car damage coverage, the car is worth more than the card&#39;s limit, the card leaves out this kind of car, or the rental is longer than the card allows. Choose <b class="gd-ui">Use OPCF 27 on my policy instead</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Ask for the Protection Plan</b> just below.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-change-my-protection" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change my protection</h2><p class="gd-p">How damage to the car is covered can be changed on your booking page, under <b class="gd-ui">Protection</b>, once you approve the offer and until you return the car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Change my protection</b>. You see the three options with their prices: your own insurance (OPCF 27), your credit card&#39;s coverage, or the CarmaCars Protection Plan.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Credit card coverage: choose your card from our list. It counts only if that card covers this car, and you tick that you will pay with it. Otherwise, OPCF 27: tick that you will upload your policy (the pink slip and the endorsement page). Otherwise, the Protection Plan.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The Protection Plan applies at once: pay the difference with <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b> on your booking. Moving off the Protection Plan needs your proof (a photo or PDF); our team checks it and the change applies once approved. You can withdraw the request while it waits.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">During your trip you can add the Protection Plan; your own insurance or card coverage is set before pickup. After damage is reported, the protection stays as it was.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-sharing-your-location-at-pickup-and-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sharing your location at pickup and return</h2><p class="gd-p">With your permission, the CarmaCars app or the website shares where you are with our team only two hours either side of your pickup and your return, so we can meet you. At any other time nothing is taken. Turn it off any time in <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Location sharing</b>.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('owner', 'notices-profile-and-leaving', 'chapter', 'for-partner-rental-companies', 'Keep your details up to date, read our notices, and know how to take a car out of the program.

## Notifications

1. Account > Notifications lists our messages: trips that are complete, payments and listing news, with your email preferences beside them. We do not email you when a booking comes in or changes, because many bookings are cancelled: the bookings coming up are always under Cars > Bookings. We email you when a trip is complete and the car is back (the dates, the days, the distance driven when it was recorded and your share of the trip; while your share is not shown to you yet, the email says it will show on your next statement), and once a week.
2. Press **Mark as read** on one, or **Mark all as read**.

![](/guides/img/owner-14-notifications-desktop-8e58b95e.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 692; address: carmacars.ca/owner/notifications; pins: 2 20.1 22.7")

## Your profile

1. Update your phone and address, then press Save. To change the email you sign in with, press **Change my email** under Sign-in: type the new address, open the link we send to it (the old address is told too), and your email changes everywhere.
2. On your agreements shows your legal name and how you are enrolled. A change to these means new agreements, so call or message us.

![](/guides/img/owner-15-profile-desktop-874dd23d.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 872; address: carmacars.ca/owner/profile; pins: 1 12.2 84.7, 2 73.4 21.2")

## Texts or email

On **Account** > **Profile**, under **Messages**, choose **Email**, **Text** or **Both**: completed trips, payouts, invoices and documents to sign by a short text with a link. Texts need a phone you verified with a code. Statements, invoices and signed documents are always emailed too. Reply STOP to any text to stop them.

## Take a car out of the program

You give 30 days'' notice for that car only. Your other cars stay in.

1. Open Cars and the car. Read Leaving: when the notice ends and what happens to your last fees.
2. Press **Give notice**. Add a Reason (optional).
3. Press **Give exit notice**. The car''s page then shows its exit date.

## Phone alerts

Get an alert on your phone or computer when one of your cars is booked, when a booking changes, for payouts and payments, incidents and documents to sign.

1. Open **Account** > **Profile**. Under **Phone alerts**, press **Turn on alerts** and allow notifications when your browser asks.
2. Under **What to alert me about**, choose the topics. Your choice applies to all your devices.
3. **Send a test alert** shows one. **Turn off on this device** stops them there; **Remove** takes another device off.

Once your application is approved, your portal asks once whether to turn alerts on: press **Turn on**, or **Not now** (it is not asked again until a later approval). On a phone, once the CarmaCars app is in the stores, the invitation offers **Download the CarmaCars app** instead.

On iPhone and iPad, add CarmaCars to your Home Screen first (Safari, **Share**, **Add to Home Screen**), then open it from there and turn alerts on. Alerts that are not urgent wait until 8 am.

## Delete my account

**Profile**, **Delete my account**, then **Yes, delete my account**. We settle your cars, payouts and invoices first (a car under your agreement leaves the program with 30 days'' notice), then delete your account and email you. **Keep my account** withdraws the request. Agreements, statements and tax records are kept as the law requires.

## Your name and password (release 34)
Open Profile. **Save my display name** changes how you are greeted, at once. Your legal name is the one on your signed agreements, so it is not edited freely: press **Request a name change**, write the full name and why, and an Admin approves it. Until then the name on file stays. To change your email, use Change my email under Sign-in; to add or change your phone, use the phone box under Sign-in (we text a code). **Change my password** sends you to the password page.

## Your week, every Monday (release 41)

Every Monday morning (about 9:00 Toronto time) you get one email, only if there was something to tell. For each car: the trips completed last week with their dates and your share (a trip whose amount is not shown to you yet says it is on your statement), your confirmed bookings in the next 14 days (dates only), and your earnings so far this month, which are provisional until your statement. Only bookings that count toward your revenue are listed. Nothing to set up; it is on by default.
