div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When you arrive, press <b class="gd-ui">End the move</b>, fill in Now at and the odometer, then press <b class="gd-ui">End the move now</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-call-and-text-the-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call and text the renter</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a card opens the Quo app with the renter&#39;s number, so the call comes from the CarmaCars number; <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> opens a small window that sends from the CarmaCars number and keeps the text with the booking.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars now</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Map of your cars</b> are links at the bottom of Today.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-start-a-handover-in-one-tap-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Start a handover in one tap (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a pickup or a return that is not started yet, the job shows <b class="gd-ui">Start the check-in now</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Start the check-out now</b>): one tap acknowledges the job, starts it and opens the one-screen handover. Not with the car yet? Press <b class="gd-ui">Acknowledge</b> so the office knows you have the job, and start it later.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-your-location-on-a-job" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your location on a job</h2><p class="gd-p">Accept the electronic monitoring policy once (you get a copy by email). While you are on shift or on a job, the CarmaCars app shares where you are so Fleet can dispatch and you can prove a pickup or return. During an active job it stays on; off duty nothing is taken. Turn it off between jobs in <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Location sharing</b>.</p></section>');
